    {
      "id": "4yga8k6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Voice – Definition"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Active Voice indicates that the subject of the sentence performs the action.",
        "Passive Voice indicates that the subject receives the action performed by the agent.",
        "Only transitive verbs (verbs taking a direct object) can be converted into Passive Voice.",
        "In Passive Voice, the main verb is always in its past participle form (V3).",
        "Imperative and Interrogative sentences follow specific structural transformation rules in passive conversions."
      ],
      "id": "y8z81fi"
    },
